# EatoBiotics — operative constraints

EatoBiotics measures a person's **food system** from a questionnaire and meal
photos, gives them a **Biotics Score™**, teaches microbiome science, and sells a
€49 Report and a €24.99/month membership. It is mid-way through a nine-stage
integrity programme (Experience 0R, six tranches done) that exists because the
product repeatedly made claims its instrument could not support.

**A great deal of this codebase is a deliberate absence, not a missing feature.**
A function returning `null`, a Report with no per-pathway breakdown, a Today
surface with no personalised verdict — these are repairs. Each carries a long
comment saying so. **Read the comment before changing the code.**

## The permanent product rule

> **Measure the food system we can observe. Teach the biology accurately. Never
> present the biology as personally measured when it isn't.**

The third clause is the one that breaks. **No surface may state, imply or render
a member's own Prebiotic, Probiotic or Postbiotic state** — not as a number, not
as a bar, not as a band word, not as a superlative, not as a possessive, not as
a mechanism ("this fed your Prebiotics"), and not as a colour, a position on a
body, or any other visual encoding. A questionnaire and a meal photo reach none
of the three.

Educational Biotics content is **preserved and improved**, never deleted. A
correction is not a deletion.

Vocabulary: **Prebiotics · Probiotics · Postbiotics** is how a score is
understood; **Feed · Seed · Rejuvenate** is how a person acts. Never equate them
in a sentence. `"heal"` is a stored key, never customer-facing. Capital-R
"Regenerate" is retired. One meal gets a **Meal** Biotics Score, never the
person's Biotics Score™.

## Hard constraints

- **Production Supabase is READ-ONLY.** Schema and data changes are **drafted,
  never applied** — commit SQL to `supabase/migrations.sql`, write the apply
  steps into the PR, a human applies it. A past authorisation is never standing
  authorisation for the next migration.
- **Only project ref `ephmojiwlcebenholhpc`.** Never read, write or name
  `hwuzbxsaxsifpdzqhqaq` or `ohwzmulsvbfgaxgziqeo` — a different product. There
  is no EatoBiotics staging project.
- **Do not modify** (`CLAUDE.md` § *What NOT to Modify*): `app/api/checkout`, `app/api/verify-payment`,
  `app/api/generate-deep-questions`, `app/api/submit-deep-assessment`,
  `app/assessment/`, `app/demo/assessment/`, `app/api/auth/`, the referral
  system (`profiles.membership`), `app/api/cms/import/chapters`. Supabase
  columns: **ADD only, never modify or drop.**
- **Never weaken a failing guard to make a suite pass.** If a guard fails,
  either the code is wrong or the guard needs a justified, measured
  recalibration recorded in writing.
- **Never delete a long explanatory comment as noise.** Several encode why a
  repair has its shape.
- **Do not DRY the three duplicated preview predicates**
  (`lib/fss/preview/preview-policy.ts`,
  `lib/report/presentation/preview-policy.ts`,
  `app/api/fss/focus-today/route.ts`). They are independent gates on independent
  unfinished features — *a shared helper is a shared switch*.
- **Never `git add -A` after running Playwright.** `docs/experience/audit/` is
  frozen before-evidence, gated on `EATOBIOTICS_AUDIT_WRITE_FROZEN=1`. Never set
  that flag.
- **Never push to `main`. No pull request unless explicitly asked.**
- **Never re-literal a price.** €49 is `REPORT_PRICE_EUR` (`lib/report/offer.ts`);
  €24.99 is `MEMBER_PRICE_EUR` (`lib/membership-tiers.ts`). Grow/Restore/Transform
  are legacy entitlements — never presented as purchasable.
- **`POST_V1_ROUTES` 404 on purpose.** Do not "fix" one by building the feature.

## The gate

Node 24 required. `next build` must precede Playwright.

```bash
npx tsc --noEmit                    # clean
npx eslint .                        # 96 problems, 0 errors
npx vitest run                      # 232 files, 6648 passed, 2 skipped
node scripts/check-ai-guard.mjs && node scripts/check-schema-drift.mjs && node scripts/check-supabase-scoping.mjs
npx next build
PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_PATH=/opt/pw-browsers/chromium-1194/chrome-linux/chrome npx playwright test   # 266
python3 tools/sabotage/run_0r.py    # 87/87 — run_s3a.py reports 2/35 by design
```

**eslint's 96 warnings are the baseline, not a to-do list.** If your change takes
it to 98, find both and fix or explain them. **Warning counts are not waivers** —
measure per file against the base commit, never infer from the total.

